  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 204 PM MDT SAT OCT 24 2026\nStrong agreement among ensemble members that an unsettled and \nactive weather pattern will set up over the region during most \nof next week. While exact details remain to be seen, there is \nstrong agreement that a period of seasonably cool and moist \nconditions will accompany this pattern change. Guidance suggests\nthat temperatures will be in the mid to upper 50s which is near\nnormal for late October. Mean precipitation values for the \nperiod are around 0.2 inches for lower valleys, 0.5 inches for \nmountain valleys, and greater than 0.6 inches for higher \nterrain. Snow levels are expected to be between 5000 to 6000 \nfeet, allowing for some early season snow accumulation.",
